-- NO-HOP CONTROL for the `export import` re-export family, re-pointed here from
-- `test/must_fail_fixtures/1369-export-import-constrained-callee-no-dict/control.mdk` when
-- RUN-XMOD-062 drained that pin.
--
-- The drained pin graded ONE verb (`run`, exit code only) on its main arm and carried this
-- control ungraded beside it. Its main arm is now the `s8-xmod-reexport-selective-
-- constrained-control/` row, which grades check + run + build + executed binary; this file
-- is the dimension that would otherwise have been lost, and it is what isolates the defect
-- to the RE-EXPORT HOP rather than to the constrained binding `f` itself: byte-identical to
-- that sibling except that it imports `lib.decl.{f}` DIRECTLY.
--
-- GROUND TRUTH, HAND-DERIVED FROM THE DECLARATION: `f : Num a => a -> a`, `f x = x + 1`,
-- instantiated at `Int` by the literal, so `f 1` = 2 on every verb.
--
-- MEASURED CORRECT ON BOTH ARMS (b313d767 and the RUN-XMOD-062 repair) -- an unchanged cell
-- on purpose. If this row ever moves, the regression is in ordinary named-import dict
-- routing and not in anything about re-exports, which is exactly what a control is for.
import lib.decl.{f}

main = println (f 1)
